The `find_zero` function finds a root of the polynomial defined by `xs`. It does this by using a binary search approach. It first finds two points `begin` and `end` such that the polynomial at `begin` and `end` have opposite signs. This is done by doubling `begin` and `end` until the polynomial at `begin` and `end` have opposite signs.

